/*
 * Parkdale Brass homepage, LIVE configuration (02 §8, 03 §9, phase-2-brief §2.3).
 * A reference copy, kept in docs/ rather than templates/ so Shopify never uploads it and Theme Check's reference
 * graph stays intact (a non-template file under templates/ adds false OrphanedSnippet warnings). At launch, copy
 * this file over templates/index.json (the comment can stay; Shopify accepts a leading comment in JSON templates),
 * or make the same changes in the theme editor. Differences from the prelaunch templates/index.json:
 *
 *   pb_hero      button "Shop jewelry" -> /collections/jewelry (was "Get launch updates" -> #signup)
 *   pb_featured  mode "collection" with the "jewelry" collection, eyebrow "Everyday essentials"; the concept
 *                blocks are removed. With no published products in "jewelry" the section renders nothing.
 *   editorial    CTA "Shop bracelets" -> /collections/bracelets (was "Be first to know" -> #signup)
 *   signup       button "Subscribe" (was "Notify me"). "consent" stays empty here, so nothing unapproved can
 *                reach the storefront: paste the owner-approved CASL wording (D-03) into it before launch.
 *                The signup form doesn't go public without it.
 *   page links   shopify://pages/our-story and shopify://pages/why-brass replace the relative /pages/ paths
 *                once those pages exist (E-03), so they follow the shopper's locale.
 *   categories   unchanged: bracelets and necklaces. Add a rings block only when D-12 lifts.
 *   journal      unchanged: "blog" "news" with "tag" "journal" (D-36), so "All articles" goes to
 *                /blogs/news/tagged/journal and stays hidden until an article has that tag (as in prelaunch).
 *                Clear the tag only once /blogs/news lists jewelry, material and care articles alone (D-11, E-07).
 *
 * Also at launch, outside this file:
 *   sections/header-group.json  remove the announcement block "announcement-bar-0" (02 §8: no announcement
 *                               unless there is a verified message).
 */
